<title>CANADA: CNR says final terms for certificates set.</title>
<headline>CNR says final terms for certificates set.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian National Railways on Tuesday said it agreed on the final terms of the US$108.3 million of pass through certificates for financing locomotive purchases.</p>
<p>The Montreal-based railway said Series-A1 of the pass through certificates, worth US$22 million, will bear 7.52 percent and mature on January 3, 2010.</p>
<p>The railway said Series-A2 of the issue, worth US$86.3 million, will bear 7.9 percent and mature on January 3, 2014.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
</text>
